  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "slam axe down, destroying all obstacles in the area",
    "skill1": "summon illusions that destroy obstacles in their path",
    "skill2": "stomp the ground to strike nearby enemies",
    "skill3": "battle max HP increase, further boosted while buff state is active",
    "skill4": "normal attacks deal bonus damage scaling on max HP",
    "skill5": "excess healing converts to permanent max HP gain"
  },
  "play_overview": "At battle start, [[Zandrok]] sends illusions charging forward that destroy obstacles and inspire passing allies with Max HP, Life Drain, and Haste. His axe slam clears leftover obstacles near the target while dealing HP-based area damage. A ground stomp hits adjacent enemies with damage that scales on Max HP, and [[Zandrok]]'s Max HP grows over the fight while inspire buffs are active. Normal attacks gain bonus damage from Max HP, and excess healing converts into permanent Max HP. He peaks on obstacle-heavy fields with healing support, but open boards waste much of the terrain value and illusion pathing.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Zandrok]] opens with an illusion charge that inspires allies with Max HP, Life Drain, and Haste, then snowballs HP-scaling damage as excess healing becomes more Max HP. Pressure [[Zandrok]] and the heal providers before the pool grows; use [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Frieren]] or [[Gwyneth]] to cut recovery. Delete this melee frontliner with high-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Perseus]], not a single-target rear pin, then finish with lasting coverage like [[Shemira]] or [[Gwyneth]]."
}
